# plans/plan_dx9.md D9-A5 scene corpus: sprite_rotated_quad
# The second SpriteBatch scene, proving D9-90's rotation/origin geometry (not just plain
# translation, which sprite_basic_quad.scene already covers). Uses a 2x2 four-color texture (not
# a 1x1 solid color) so a 90-degree rotation is independently verifiable: a clean, exact
# rotation angle (cos(90 deg)=0, sin(90 deg)=1, no fractional trig involved) around the texture's
# own CENTER as origin, with a SQUARE (not rectangular) destination so the rotation doesn't
# change the bounding box at all -- only which color ends up in which corner.
#
# Real XNA's SpriteBatch rotation formula (SpriteBatch.cs's own GenerateVertexInfo, confirmed
# against FNA's transcription of it, same rotate-then-translate-around-origin shape this
# project's own D3D11SpriteBatchRenderer already implements): a positive rotation angle rotates
# CLOCKWISE on screen (screen Y increases downward, so the standard mathematical CCW convention
# with Y-up becomes CW with Y-down) -- confirmed empirically here, not assumed, since this is the
# oracle's own job.
#
# Texture (row-major, top row first): top-left=RED, top-right=GREEN / bottom-left=BLUE,
# bottom-right=YELLOW. Origin = (1,1), the exact texture center (matches a 2x2 texture's own
# center point in texel space). destinationRectangle = (88,88,80,80) -- a square centered on
# (128,128), so rotation only permutes which quadrant shows which color, the bounding box stays
# fixed. rotation = pi/2 (90 degrees).
width=256
height=256
profile=HiDef
clearcolor=100,149,237,255
spritebatchmode=true
texturewidth=2
textureheight=2
texturepixel=255,0,0,255
texturepixel=0,255,0,255
texturepixel=0,0,255,255
texturepixel=255,255,0,255
spritedestrect=88,88,80,80
spritecolor=255,255,255,255
spriterotation=1.5707963267948966
spriteorigin=1,1
